<title>GERMANY: Bundesbank sets next two repos at fixed 3.00 pct.</title>
<headline>Bundesbank sets next two repos at fixed 3.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Thursday that its policy-making council had decided to set the next two securities repurchase rate, or repo, tenders at a fixed rate of three percent.</p>
<p>The bank's main money market rate has been held steady at three percent since August.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
